Package: walden
Version: @VERSION@-@DEB_REVISION@
Architecture: @DEB_ARCHITECTURE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @DEB_INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Depends: systemd, nftables, libc6, curl
Description: @DEB_SYNOPSIS@
 Walden blocks the websites named in a small user-owned configuration file for
 a period fixed when the block starts. The wait cannot be shortened or
 cancelled, and the block outlives logging out, restarting the machine, and
 removing this package.
 .
 A privileged daemon enforces the block through /etc/hosts and nftables. The
 package installs that daemon inactive and leaves its systemd unit disabled:
 it runs only while a block does.
